164
00:14:56,814 --> 00:14:59,923
The assignment has three questions. One:

165
00:14:59,943 --> 00:15:04,616
a T-shirt line has 8 operations and a target of 150 an hour.

166
00:15:04,636 --> 00:15:08,761
Find takt and the theoretical minimum, the headcount,

167
00:15:08,781 --> 00:15:12,437
cycle and balance with one operation per group,

168
00:15:12,457 --> 00:15:16,661
and then your own grouping under this lecture's rules.

169
00:15:17,061 --> 00:15:23,697
Two: 'set sleeves' was timed ten times at an average of 0.52 minutes,

170
00:15:23,717 --> 00:15:30,448
rated 90 percent, with 15 percent allowance. Find the standard minute,

171
00:15:30,468 --> 00:15:38,358
and explain what a rating of 110 percent would do to line balance and piece rates.

172
00:15:38,758 --> 00:15:46,330
Three: a pattern sewer takes 0.25 minutes to load, 0.05 to walk and 1.0 to sew;

173
00:15:46,350 --> 00:15:52,577
wages are 0.5 yuan a minute and machines 0.10 per machine-minute.

174
00:15:52,597 --> 00:15:59,978
Find the balance point, the cycle and cost per piece for 3, 4 and 5 machines,

175
00:15:59,998 --> 00:16:07,378
choose the cheapest, and say how the answer changes if loading drops to 0.15.

176
00:16:07,778 --> 00:16:12,257
Submit the assignment and the lab report on the WenQuest platform.

177
00:16:13,777 --> 00:16:17,853
There's also a ten-question quiz. For example:

178
00:16:17,873 --> 00:16:24,086
an operation's observed time averages 0.50 minutes, rated 105 percent,

179
00:16:24,106 --> 00:16:28,894
with 12 percent allowance. What's the standard minute?

180
00:16:29,294 --> 00:16:37,596
Or: a garment takes 15.6 minutes of work in all, and the target is 100 an hour.

181
00:16:37,616 --> 00:16:41,914
What's the theoretical minimum headcount?

182
00:16:42,314 --> 00:16:47,459
You get three attempts, and the explanations appear as soon as you submit.

183
00:16:48,979 --> 00:16:50,285
Three things to remember.

184
00:16:50,685 --> 00:16:58,963
One: a standard minute is observed time times rating times one plus allowance;

185
00:16:58,983 --> 00:17:04,814
most of it is handling, so more top speed helps little.

186
00:17:05,214 --> 00:17:09,281
Two: takt, minimum headcount, cycle and balance;

187
00:17:09,301 --> 00:17:13,283
one operation per station wastes odd fractions,

188
00:17:13,303 --> 00:17:20,350
while grouping by positional weight lifts balance from about 70 to over 90 percent.

189
00:17:20,750 --> 00:17:26,973
Three: in multi-machine tending the cycle is the larger of the two;

190
00:17:26,993 --> 00:17:28,557
choose n by cost.

191
